{"availability":"available","full":"beingforthebenefit/Bandstand","name":"Bandstand","description":"A request portal to propose songs for Monkee Business","category":"Business","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2025-08-30T14:17:24Z","updated":"2026-10-09T15:06:21Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://beingforthebenefit.github.io/Bandstand/","topics":[],"demo":"https://beingforthebenefit.github.io/Bandstand/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:39:28.740Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T15:39:28.740Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T15:39:28.740Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T15:39:28.740Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Bandstand: a self-hosted hub for bands — chord charts with full version history, setlists, a stage performance mode, rehearsal availability, and song proposals. One install serves several bands; each can have its own name, icon and web address. Built with Next.js, NextAuth, Prisma/Postgres and Vitest. It started as Monkee Wrench, the hub for Monkee Business (still its name there), live at .","Product page: (from site/, published by CI with each push to main; its screenshots come from scripts/site-shots.mjs)."],"features":["Charts: every song's chart is ChordPro text, rendered as chords over lyrics. Transpose and text size are remembered per device. Every section is always written out in full — no \"same as verse 1\".","History: every save is a new version with author, date and an optional note; a musician-readable diff between versions; a PDF of any version; admins can restore (which saves a new version, so nothing is lost). Two…","PDFs: generated on request — one song in any key, or a whole setlist in order with each song's set key and note. Letter or A4. The footer stamps the version and editor, so an old printout is obvious.","Setlists: drag (or up/down) to reorder, a key and a note per song (e.g. vocal assignments). Admins can delete a setlist from its edit page.","Performance mode (/perform/:id): chart-only, two layouts with a toggle in the header (remembered per device). Pages (default on iPad/desktop): fitted to the screen in columns; long songs page instead of shrinking.…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/beingforthebenefit/Bandstand/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"66a4ce5696ea9ed1bc669b3d45cfd26bc9428f0393ad300f30b4456842d70a17","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T15:39:28.970Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T15:39:28.970Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Bandstand: a self-hosted hub for bands — chord charts with full version history, setlists, a stage performance mode, rehearsal availability, and song proposals. One install serves several bands; each can have its own name, icon and web address. Built with Next.js, NextAuth, Prisma/Postgres and Vitest. It started as Monkee Wrench, the hub for Monkee Business (still its name there), live at .","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/beingforthebenefit/Bandstand/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"A web address can belong to a band: its sign-in page, title, favicon and home-screen icon are that band's.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/beingforthebenefit/Bandstand/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Everything except sign-in requires an account (charts are copyrighted).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/beingforthebenefit/Bandstand/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"66a4ce5696ea9ed1bc669b3d45cfd26bc9428f0393ad300f30b4456842d70a17","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/beingforthebenefit/Bandstand/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T15:39:28.970Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T15:06:21Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/beingforthebenefit/Bandstand/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T15:39:28.972Z","hash":"66a4ce5696ea9ed1bc669b3d45cfd26bc9428f0393ad300f30b4456842